invariant: INV-33
file: webpki_pin.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh webpki_pin
reason: copy_key copies one byte more than the key the reader decoded, so a
  key of CH_WEBPKI_KEY_MAX bytes writes one byte past webpki_leaf_info.key.
  The byte stays inside the struct, so no object-level check sees it; the
  webpki_pin proof's stub of this one memcpy asserts the copy fits the key
  field, and fails here.

--- old
    memcpy(out->key, key->key, key->key_len);
--- new
    memcpy(out->key, key->key, key->key_len + 1);
